  "lineage": "Korean solo form in which a performer sings pansori excerpts and short folk-derived songs while simultaneously accompanying herself on the twelve-string gayageum, developed in the late nineteenth century out of the sanjo circle around Kim Chang-jo and carried into the twentieth by Oh Tae-seok, Park Gwi-hui and Kang Jeong-suk — the zither punctuating rather than doubling the vocal line, both parts riding a janggu jangdan cycle in jinyang, jungmori or jajinmori, with the gruff pansori chest voice and wide yukjabaegi vibrato intact.",
